{
  "description": "The goal is to discover materials with high carbon dioxide (CO2) uptake among the available mol_ids. CO2 uptake describes how much carbon dioxide a material adsorbs under specified conditions. It matters when identifying materials for carbon capture and gas storage.\n\nThe target is simulated CO2 uptake, expressed in mol/kg (moles of CO2 per kilogram of MOF), at 298 K and 0.15 bar. Higher values mean greater CO2 uptake under these conditions.\n\nThe candidate materials are metal-organic frameworks (MOFs).",
